{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788313008,"nonce":"i59YCM5HNvObcANDEVTUxb5/d3U=","message":"Found in play, m1-20260901, tick ~255,000 (Spring day 10, run day ~4.4). Evan, after unblocking it by hand: *\"we forgot to handle naming.\"* The verb-level half is filed separately as **`5cb1f9f`** (p0) — `dialog-dismiss` closes a text-entry dialog without answering it, so the prompt re-raised every 1,000 ticks and wedged the run. This comment is the other half, and it belongs here rather than in a new issue.\n\n**`checklists/triggered.md` §Colony start has 12 numbered steps and none of them is \"name the faction and the settlement.\"** Nor does `playbook/SESSION-START.md`'s 10-position load order, nor `PLAY-LOOP.md` §Halts, which treats `reason:\"dialog\"` as an *event* to handle when it arrives rather than as a scheduled obligation of every new colony.\n\nThat framing is what made it a surprise. Every colony start raises `Dialog_NamePlayerFactionAndSettlement`, it is `forcePause`, and it does not arrive at tick 0 — on this run it arrived at ~255,000, four in-game days in, long after the colony-start section had been run and logged complete. So the checklist read as fully discharged while a mandatory step was still outstanding, and the thing that eventually surfaced it was a wedge rather than a check.\n\nThree specific consequences for 4.2:\n\n1. **A colony-start step can fall due long after colony start.** The section is written as \"run it top to bottom on any fresh colony, before the first advance\", and this step cannot be run then — the window does not exist yet. Either the section grows a class of deferred items with a trigger (`triggered.md`'s own act/event vocabulary already has the shape), or naming gets an event trigger of its own and the colony-start list cross-references it.\n2. **`PLAY-LOOP.md`'s dialog rule needs the periodic case.** It currently branches on \"dialog verbs exist\" versus \"they do not\", and neither branch fits: the verbs exist, `dialog-dismiss` reports success, and the dialog comes back. The wedge rule it relies on — two consecutive advances returning `ticks_elapsed: 0` — does not fire, because each of these advances ran a full 1,000 ticks. A dialog that is answered-looking but not answered is worse than one that refuses.\n3. **The invariant list says \"no human input beyond watching.\"** Naming made that false on this run: Evan typed the name in the window. Until `5cb1f9f` ships, any unattended run reaching the naming prompt stops there, and 4.2's acceptance (\"a scripted one-day session on a fixture colony\") never reaches it — a one-day session ends before tick 255,000, which is exactly why this survived every acceptance pass so far.\n\n\n- `triggered.md` §Colony start gains the naming step, marked as deferred-with-a-trigger rather than a pre-first-advance item, citing `5cb1f9f` for the verb it needs.\n- `PLAY-LOOP.md` §Halts gains the third dialog branch: a force-pausing window that re-raises after a successful dismiss is a wedge, reported as one, with the window type named. Suggested detector: N consecutive `dialog` halts on the same window type, independent of `ticks_elapsed`.\n- `accept/4.2-play-loop.py` gains a check that the run's ledger contains the naming step once the item exists — the no-silent-skips diff, extended to deferred items.\n- The invariant \"no human input beyond watching\" is either qualified or `5cb1f9f` becomes a dependency of any unattended-run claim. This run reports the intervention explicitly rather than quietly.","files":null}]}